                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d5561bd-d210-378b-9818-02a49b0ecfa0",
                        "entry_id": "7fc057de-dbf4-39f7-adbc-d61aff51708e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "człowiek bardzo dokładny, przywiązujący dużą wagę do porządku"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f414a5e-cdf4-47b2-86f2-84d13d2979b9",
                                "sense_id": "8d5561bd-d210-378b-9818-02a49b0ecfa0",
                                "text": "Ja jestem pedantem, a moja żona to straszna bałaganiara."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b2f7ffe-bb28-4be6-ab14-183db7ca26e1",
                        "source_entry_id": "7fc057de-dbf4-39f7-adbc-d61aff51708e",
                        "source_sense_id": "8d5561bd-d210-378b-9818-02a49b0ecfa0",
                        "target_lang_word": "pedant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pedant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b670bf75-26f6-3fdd-8fa0-127bce62b7e0",
                                        "entry_id": "28f6655b-9958-3303-822d-75c5241bf019",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who makes an excessive or tedious show of their knowledge, especially regarding rules of vocabulary and grammar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39c719c3-978e-3648-a405-c005e502660b",
                                        "entry_id": "28f6655b-9958-3303-822d-75c5241bf019",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who is overly concerned with formal rules and trivial points of learning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "239882e1-0e19-3b7a-a699-c3ca15683f85",
                                        "entry_id": "28f6655b-9958-3303-822d-75c5241bf019",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A teacher or schoolmaster."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89c518cf-f3c4-4935-994f-f777eb6eb40b",
                                                "sense_id": "239882e1-0e19-3b7a-a699-c3ca15683f85",
                                                "text": "I have in my youth oftentimes beene vexed to see a Pedant [tr. pedante] brought in, in most of Italian comedies, for a vice or sport-maker, and the nicke-name of Magister to be of no better signification amongst us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pedant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65f8ec39-1be9-345d-9369-92daf1b6fabb",
                                        "entry_id": "df5839f0-adca-376f-b645-161e92e26ae1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pedantic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pedant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                        "entry_id": "35695c90-b30b-34f9-ae4e-b7dab461e6cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be or act as a pedant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "humorous",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ce1651c-005d-4bb6-b22b-55835b122c58",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "[…] as any occasion of going behond^([sic – meaning beyond]) the sea with sombody, or pedanting in some Gentlemans house, &c., for clergy-employment I will accept of none."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "152bab8b-a47b-4971-a6fa-eaf2598e422c",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "Tediously he pedanted, hedging around concerning the Perfect State, eventually coming out into the open with his own private Perfect State plan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff601915-bda0-474c-9250-bd25f7b0dac8",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "‘Most people in this country aren’t Christian, the standard package should not be Christian,’ Gerrard pedanted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24e062f8-3ae0-4987-90c8-5b76e231cfb9",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "Jim’s mother pestered him daily for a month to come home for a talk. At first he rejected the offer, knowing what to expect, dear old dad would dance around the room pedanting about some shit that didn’t make sense anyway."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4c4439f-2073-4965-a9db-12dcacac96c9",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "“Okay,” she said to the investigators, “how can I help you?” / “You, uhh, wouldn’t happen to have seven bodies lying around, would you?” Bao Bai-Leung, feeling a little ridiculous, asked. “Maybe in…your closet?” / “As I under stand human Anna to my,”^([sic]) Blarcch Beletchian pedanted at them, “there is not enough room for bodies to lie in a small space like a closet. Unless they were midgets like this person, or their limbs were detachable, or the closet was a gateway to eleven-dimensional space, or –” / “Oh, great!” TOM put in. “We got a literalist, here!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da196762-efcd-425c-b8b0-cee5b89e0431",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "So, why do pedants pedant? We don’t really know, but some tangential studies infer it’s to do with a mixture of personality, status-signalling and group identification."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99a6a667-eb77-4e27-9938-afc0c272c066",
                                                "sense_id": "45f5f0a2-05fd-32e9-8166-562f13f4d728",
                                                "text": "When one Oxford fellow was ejected in 1648 he immediately wrote to his royalist patron seeking employment ‘going behond [sic] the sea with sombody, or pedanting in some Gentlemans house’.¹²⁸ Whether he succeeded or not is not known, but others certainly ended up ‘pedanting’."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1544ba4-ccdc-4196-9c34-ec9f867db8bc",
                        "source_entry_id": "7fc057de-dbf4-39f7-adbc-d61aff51708e",
                        "source_sense_id": "8d5561bd-d210-378b-9818-02a49b0ecfa0",
